From cdc3e10c49e25a50109910e906f5dca806003ea0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Kesling <alex@kesling.co>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:49:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add a GDB remote probe: --probe gdb:HOST:PORT

For targets with no debug probe at all, an emulator chiefly. The core
speaks the GDB remote serial protocol and asks a little more of the
server than GDB itself does: memory reads and writes while the target
runs, as a probe makes them over the AHB-AP, and register numbers that
are ARMRegister's DCRSR selectors. The target is left running on attach;
halt and run are ^C and `c`.

It is wired into attach_live and attach_live_or_dump ahead of the USB
probes, so it works in a build without the "probes" feature. It sets no
socket timeouts, because the server it exists for runs under kernels
(zaqaru's) that refuse SO_RCVTIMEO.
